For each slot, the enforced order is previous consumer completion → next producer → ready event → next consumer → consumed event. The producer owns the slot for writing until ready completes; the consumer then owns it for reading until consumed completes, after which the next producer may overwrite it. Every wait is submitted after its intended event recording and before that event’s next re-recording, so event reuse does not change already-captured dependencies. Separate result entries prevent output overwrites, and the final B-stream synchronization implies every consumer and its prerequisite producer has finished before verification and cleanup. There is no device-wide synchronization and no host synchronization between iterations.

