The precise `__shfl_sync` contracts are:
- Each caller must have its own bit set in the mask.
- All non-exited threads named in that mask must execute the corresponding shuffle with the same mask; different callers may specify different source lanes.
- The requested source must actively participate in that collective. Reading an inactive or nonparticipating source yields an undefined value.
- With width 32 and source 18, the source is physical lane 18 within the warp. The mask does not compact or renumber lanes.

Compute membership before divergence with a full-warp ballot, then let only lanes 0–18 execute the shuffle:

```cpp
#include <cuda_runtime.h>

__device__ float broadcast_lane18(float value)
{
    const unsigned linearThread =
        threadIdx.x + blockDim.x *
        (threadIdx.y + blockDim.y * threadIdx.z);
    const unsigned lane = linearThread % 32u;
    const bool participates = lane <= 18u;

    const unsigned mask =
        __ballot_sync(0xffffffffu, participates);

    if (participates) {
        value = __shfl_sync(mask, value, 18, 32);
    }
    return value;
}
```

